es its metadata: only a member that\n  1211\t   claimed coverage finalizes a side table, whatever its siblings\n  1212\t   claimed.\"\n  1213\t  [batch]\n  1214\t  (nth batch 5 nil))\n  1215\t\n  1216\t\n  1217\t(defn- final-call-site-metadata\n  1218\t  \"The call-site occurrence contract's (C1) side table of an expanded\n  1219\t   final tree, as frontend-metadata rows `[origin root path\n  1220\t   :yang/call-site 1]` in printed-row order: one row per\n  1221\t   `:application` occurrence of the stand-in-lowered, tail-marked tree\n  1222\t   that actually executes. The frontend's own markers named the\n  1223\t   pre-expansion tree; expansion, tail marking and stand-in lowering\n  1224\t   recompute roots and paths, so no pre-expansion table can cover this\n  1225\t   tree and the table is finalized here, over the finished rows. The\n  1226\t   origin is the run member's admission origin — the same coordinate\n  1227\t   the expander's event rows carry for a top-level frame. No\n  1228\t   expansion-record address is fabricated for the batch as a whole:\n  1229\t   the batch's attempts are individually recorded in the log, and the\n  1230\t   final tree is their admitted input's finished form.\"\n  1231\t  [row-set origin]\n  1232\t  (vec (sort-by pr-str\n  1233\t                (map (fn [[root path]] [origin root path :yang/call-site 1])\n  1234\t                     (vm/application-occurrences row-set)))))\n  1235\t\n  1236\t\n  1237\t(defn expand-batch\n  1238\t  \"Expand one input batch against `ctx` (§3.2). Returns\n  1239\t   `{:status :ok :tree packet :log log :ctx ctx'}` or\n  1240\t   `{:status :error :error e :log log :ctx ctx'}`. Either way `ctx'` has\n  1241\t   consumed the batch (`:t` + 1) and every attempt it allocated; only\n  1242\t   success changes the store, to the post-harvest store. A success also\n  1243\t   carries `:frontend-metadata` — the C1 side table finalized over the\n  1244\t   final tree (`final-call-site-metadata`), covering the tree that\n  1245\t   actually executes — when, and only when, the selected member itself\n  1246\t   claimed C1 coverage (its own verdict in `batch-call-site-claims`); a\n  1247\t   sibling's claim never manufactures a table for it, and an unclaimed\n  1248\t   batch carries no table at all, never an empty one. The table's\n  1249\t   occurrence origin rides beside it as `:call-site-origin`, the\n  1250\t   admission this expansion produced the tree under (§2.1). A context\n  1251\t   store binding a\n  1252\t   reserved name, or holding an entry without the current AST contract,\n  1253\t   is refused (Rule R): it is a composition defect, so it throws rather\n  1254\t   than returning an error.\"\n  1255\t  [batch ctx]\n  1256\t  (check-store! (:store ctx))\n  1257\t  (let [ctx (with-default-guards ctx)\n  1258\t        source-batch (:t ctx)\n  1259\t        base {:ctx ctx, :source-batch source-batch, :events [], :produced []}\n  1260\t        finish (fn [st]\n  1261\t                 (let [ctx' (update (:ctx st) :t inc)]\n  1262\t                   (if-let [e (:error st)]\n  1263\t                     {:status :error, :error e, :log (log-packet st), :ctx ctx'}\n  1264\t                     {:status :ok, :tree (:tree st), :log (log-packet st),\n  1265\t                      :frontend-metadata (:frontend-metadata st),\n  1266\t                      :call-site-origin (:call-site-origin st),\n  1267\t                      :ctx (assoc ctx' :store (:next-store st))})))\n  1268\t        {:keys [admitted error]} (admit batch)]\n  1269\t    (if error\n  1270\t      (let [[st counter] (allocate-attempt base)]\n  1271\t        (finish (-> st\n  1272\t                    (record-event (event-row (attempt-id ctx counter) source-batch\n  1273\t                                             (source-origin ctx source-batch nil)\n  1274\t                                             nil nil nil nil nil error))\n  1275\t                    (fail error))))\n  1276\t      (let [{:keys 